# Planning workflow

This project follows a strict pipeline. Skipping a stage is a review-blocker.

```
0. General plan        -> plan/0-general-architecture.md
1. Use case detail     -> plan/{N}-{scope}.md
2. Architecture        -> ports, adapters, module layout (in the same plan file)
3. E2E tests (BDD)     -> tests/e2e/features/*.feature (+ step defs)
4. Functional tests    -> tests/functional/*.rs (per use case)
5. Implementation      -> src/**/*.rs
```

## Rules

- Do not open a coding PR without an accepted plan section. If a behaviour is not
  in `plan/`, propose a plan edit first.
- Tests come before code. Functional tests must compile and fail for the right
  reason (unimplemented) before any production code is written for that use case.
- Every use case must map 1:1 to a file under
  `src/application/use_cases/{snake_case_use_case}.rs` and appear in at least one
  `.feature` scenario.
- Every port defined in a plan file must exist as a trait under
  `src/application/ports/{snake_case_port}.rs` with a doc comment referencing the
  plan section (for example `/// See plan/6-address-detail.md#5-ports-required`).
- Every adapter method must reference the exact Alchemy / Etherscan / openchain /
  Samczsun endpoint it targets in its doc comment.
- The plan is the source of truth. When the code and the plan disagree, fix the
  plan first and then the code.
- Plan files are English-only. Same for code, comments, test names and commit
  messages.

## When proposing a new feature

1. Ask whether it should become a new `plan/{N}-{scope}.md` file, a new section in
   an existing file, or the "Deferred" section of `plan/README.md`.
2. If new file: use the template from `plan/README.md` section "How to add a new
   plan file".
3. List the use cases, ports, data sources, BDD scenarios, functional tests and
   fixtures before writing any code.
